{
  "assumptions": [
    "176 Transmetro + 93 TuBus are user-requested fixed scenario counts, not measured simultaneous in-domain traffic and not official operator fleet allocation.",
    "Line allocations are synthetic largest remainders of the historical per-system quotas, with service_id ascending ties; they are not an observed sector allocation.",
    "N counts cars, motorcycles and freight, excluding public vehicles and internal transit drivers. B=269 is fixed even for N=0 and N=1000; it does not mean simultaneous traffic or 24-hour service.",
    "Schedules are weekday operating windows, not published headways. Departures are derived from finite reusable vehicle rosters.",
    "L12 closes at 22:00 by user scenario instruction; an external secondary timetable lists 21:00. This is not reconciled as fact.",
    "Download coverage/network is the computational domain, not a verified administrative Zona 1 polygon.",
    "Exterior circulation and depot time are timed off-network activities, assumed 1800s; local terminal turns 180s. No exterior trajectory or speed is invented.",
    "Four dated OSM bus relation directions contradict generic one-way tags on three ways. Activating these bus-only directions requires explicit --accept-transit-route-assumptions.",
    "TuBus104/105/802 paths are directed bounded GIS map matches. 802 uses reversed vertex order consistent with local printed stop order and road direction.",
    "TuBus305 is not included because the supplied source does not establish a path in this domain. Its vehicles are not invented.",
    "Stops without a spatial source remain unmodeled; endpoint gateway facilities are not passenger stops. Dwell is 25s assumed; stop coordinates may be link endpoint proxies.",
    "Bus articulation, passengers, boarding demand and calibrated fleet frequencies are not modeled. Vehicles use rigid envelopes 13.5m/12m by 2.5m.",
    "An actual delayed bus is never duplicated to meet a planned departure. New departures stop at closing; active trips may finish afterwards and are reported separately."
  ],
